{
	id: basics-01
	version: 1
	kind: tutorial
	title: The Basics: Companions and Skirmishes
	summary: Learn about guiding your Ring-bearer through sites, and defend against a swarm of Orcs along the way.
	author: ketura
	tags: basics, phases, twilight, archery, assignment, skirmish, overwhelm, events, sanctuary, defender
	format: scenario
	human: freeps
	opponent: {
		name: Basic Shadow
		fallback: pass
	}
	coverage: strict
	options: {
		autoPass: archery, assignment, regroup
	}
	cards: {
		freeps: {
			# Frodo, Resolute Hobbit
			frodo: 10_121
			# The One Ring, The Ruling Ring
			ring: 1_2
			# Gandalf, The Grey Pilgrim
			gandalf: 2_122
			# Servant of the Secret Fire
			servant1: 1_83
			# Servant of the Secret Fire
			servant2: 1_83
			# Swordarm of the White Tower
			swordarm1: 1_116
			# Swordarm of the White Tower
			swordarm2: 1_116
			# Noble Intentions
			noble1: 1_304
			# Aragorn, Heir of Elendil
			aragorn: 4_109
			# Boromir, Steward's Heir
			boromir: 0_65
			# Noble Intentions
			noble2: 1_304
		}
		shadow: {
			# Frodo, Resolute Hobbit
			oppFrodo: 10_121
			# Goblin Bowman
			bowman: 2_60
			# Mordor Soldier
			soldier: 7_290
			# Ancient Chieftain
			chieftain: 1_163
			# Drums in the Deep
			drums1: 1_168
			# Goblin Runner
			runner1: 1_178
			# Goblin Runner
			runner2: 1_178
			# Goblin Bowman
			bowman2: 2_60
			# Goblin Marksman
			marksman: 1_176
			# Moria Scout
			scout: 1_191
			# Host of Moria, Legion of the Underdeeps
			host: 9_41
		}
	}
	ringBearer: {
		freeps: frodo
		shadow: oppFrodo
	}
	ring: {
		freeps: ring
	}
	# Green Hill Country, Breeland Forest, Rivendell Valley, Great Chasm
	sites: {
		freeps: 1_323, 1_329, 1_341, 2_118
		shadow: 1_323, 1_329, 1_341, 2_118
	}
	rules: {
		oneSided: true
		freeps: [
			{
				type: modifier
				modifier: {
					type: modifyHandSize
					amount: -3
				}
			}
			{
				type: modifier
				modifier: {
					type: disableGameText
					filter: name(The One Ring)
				}
			}
			{
				type: modifier
				modifier: {
					type: skipPhase
					phase: maneuver
				}
			}
		]
		shadow: [
			{
				type: modifier
				modifier: {
					type: modifyRoamingPenalty
					filter: minion
					amount: -2
				}
			}
		]
	}
	setup: {
		shadow: {
			hand: bowman
		}
	}
	outcome: {
		lose: {
			type: hasCardInDeadPile
			filter: companion
		}
		loseMessage: One of your companions has fallen, but there was a way for all companions to make it through. Go back to the last checkpoint and look at the numbers again: who is about to be overwhelmed, and which card in your hand can stop it?  The order you perform your skirmishes in can sometimes be important as well.
	}
	steps: [
		# ---- 1
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(1)
			messages: [
				{
					header: Welcome to the Lord of the Rings Trading Card Game!
					text: "In this tutorial series, you will play through several scenarios which will teach you the mechanics of the game and the interface here on Gemp.  \n\nThe rules will be simplified from the real game to help you learn, but as you progress we will slowly mix in the real rules until you're ready to face real players.\n\nLet's get started!"
				}
				{
					text: "This is Frodo.  He is your **Ring-bearer**.  The Ring-bearer is your most important character; if he dies or falls to temptation, **you lose the game**.  \n\nUnderneath him, Frodo bears..."
					anchor: card:frodo
					highlight: card:frodo
				}
				{
					text: ...The One Ring!  This is a special card with special rules, but all you need to remember for now is that your Ring-bearer holds it and keeps it safe from the forces of evil.
					anchor: card:ring
					highlight: card:ring
					avoid: card:frodo, ui:alertBox, zone:self.support
				}
				{
					text: "This is a **Site** card.  It is placed horizontally and represents where your Ring-bearer currently is in the wide world of Middle-earth.  \n\nToday we start the game at **[[Green Hill Country]]**."
					anchor: ui:site:1
					highlight: ui:site:1
					avoid: ui:twilightPool, ui:advPath, ui:phase, zone:opp.support, zone:opp.characters
				}
				{
					text: "This is the **Adventure Path**.  Frodo will have to journey through 9 sites on his way to destroy the Ring, getting as close to Mount Doom as he can.  \n\nIf your Ring-bearer survives combat on Site 9, you win!\n\nIn this tutorial, we will journey through 4 sites."
					anchor: ui:advPath
					highlight: ui:advPath
				}
				{
					text: "On Gemp, you can hover over cards with your mouse to get a readable preview of the card.  You can also right-click (or swipe up on mobile devices) to open a card preview window.  \n\nRight-click on Frodo now."
					anchor: card:frodo
					highlight: card:frodo
					advance: inspect(frodo)
				}
				{
					text: "Here you can see the text on the card, as well as a readout that tells you all the different effects which are altering Frodo's state.  In some games, you'll need to view this screen a lot!  \n\nClick outside this window or press ESC to dismiss it."
					anchor: ui:cardInfo
					advance: close
				}
				{
					text: "The game is divided into **Phases**.  Keep an eye on this area as gameplay advances.\n\nRight now, it is the **Fellowship Phase**, but Frodo is all alone and has no equipment for you to play."
					anchor: ui:phase
					highlight: ui:phase
				}
				{
					text: "Frodo is going to start his journey, so we will go with him!  \n\nClick Pass to end the Fellowship Phase and move to the next site."
					anchor: ui:button:pass
					highlight: ui:button:pass
				}
			]
			allow: pass
		}
		# ---- 2
		{
			when: opponent, action, phase(shadow), turn(1)
			messages: [
				{
					text: Frodo has traveled to the **[[Breeland Forest]]** for Site 2.  When traveling, we attract the attention of the forces of Shadow.
					anchor: ui:site:2
					highlight: ui:site:2
					side: below
				}
				{
					text: This is the **Twilight Pool**.  It represents how much attention Frodo has drawn.  The more Twilight is added to the pool, the more resources your opponent will have to punish you.
					anchor: ui:twilightPool
					highlight: ui:twilightPool
				}
				{
					text: "Each time you move to a new site, you will add (1) twilight token per companion in your fellowship.  \n\nYou will also add twilight equal to the new site's **Shadow Number**, shown here in the black orb in the upper right."
					zoom: site:2
					focus: shadowNumber
				}
			]
			answer: play(bowman)
		}
		# ---- 3
		{
			note: The opponent has nothing left to play.  It is asked all the same, because this step is about its pass: that is what lets something be said while it is still the Shadow phase.
			when: opponent, action, phase(shadow), turn(1)
			messages: [
				{
					text: It is now the **Shadow Phase**, and your opponent is sending creatures to hunt down Frodo.
					anchor: card:bowman
					highlight: card:bowman, ui:twilightPool
				}
				{
					text: This [[Goblin Bowman]] costs {cost:bowman} twilight, which has been removed from the Twilight Pool, leaving {twilight} remaining.
					highlight: ui:twilightPool
					zoom: card:bowman
					focus: cost
				}
			]
			answer: pass
		}
		# ---- 4
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(archery), turn(1)
			messages: [
				{
					text: After the Shadow player has finished making actions, we move on to other phases.  Now we are at the **Archery Phase**.
					anchor: ui:phase
					highlight: ui:phase
				}
				{
					text: This Goblin has the bold keyword **Archer** in its game text, which means it will automatically fire one arrow at us at the end of the phase.  More archers means more arrows, but for now there's only one.
					anchor: card:bowman
					highlight: card:bowman:text, ui:phase
				}
				During each phase, both players will have an opportunity to make actions keyed to that phase, back and forth, until both players pass.
				{
					text: You don't have any archery actions of your own, so click Pass.
					anchor: ui:button:pass
					highlight: ui:button:pass
				}
			]
			allow: pass
		}
		# ---- 5
		{
			when: freeps, assign, turn(1)
			messages: [
				{
					text: Ouch!  Frodo has taken an arrow.  That **wound** is represented with a red bead.
					anchor: card:frodo:wounds
					highlightStyle: red
					avoid: card:frodo, zone:minions
					side: right
				}
				{
					text: Frodo's **Vitality** is shown in the red orb.  If he takes this many wounds, he will die, and his quest will fail.
					anchor: card:frodo
					highlight: card:frodo:vitality
					highlightStyle: red
					zoom: card:frodo
					focus: vitality
				}
				{
					text: Gemp will automatically update the numbers on card stats for you to help you keep track.  Frodo's 4 vitality has been reduced by his 1 wound, showing 3 remaining.
					anchor: card:frodo:vitality
					highlight: card:frodo:vitality
					avoid: ui:advPath, ui:alertBox, zone:self.support
					side: right
					gap: 12
				}
				{
					text: "After Archery, we move to skirmish combat.\n\nDuring the **Assignment Phase**, you will choose who fights who.  Every minion must be assigned to one of your companions.  \n\nClick on the Goblin to assign it."
					anchor: card:bowman
					avoid: card:frodo
				}
				{
					text: Once clicked, you will have to choose who will fight that minion.  Frodo is the only companion you have, so select him.
					anchor: card:frodo
					on: picked(bowman)
				}
				{
					text: There are no other minions to assign, so lock in your assignments by clicking Done.
					anchor: ui:button:done
					on: ready
				}
			]
			allow: assign(frodo: bowman)
		}
		# ---- 6
		{
			when: freeps, cards, text(next skirmish), turn(1)
			messages: [
				{
					text: "Now we move on to the **Skirmish Phase**.  Every assigned pair of characters will fight in their own individual battle.  \n\nClick on Frodo to begin his skirmish."
					anchor: ui:assignment:frodo
				}
			]
			allow: choose(frodo)
		}
		# ---- 7
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(skirmish), turn(1)
			messages: [
				{
					text: "Skirmishes are a contest of **Strength**. Strength is the number on the brown shield icon, and represents battle prowess.  Whoever has more strength wins the skirmish.  \n\nFrodo's strength is increased by the One Ring, putting him from 3 to 4.\n\nBut right now, both sides are tied!  Shadow plays dirty, so minions always win skirmish ties."
					anchor: ui:skirmish
					highlight: card:frodo:strength, card:bowman:strength
				}
				{
					text: You don't have any skirmish actions, so click Pass to end the skirmish.
					anchor: ui:button:pass
					highlight: ui:button:pass
				}
			]
			allow: pass
		}
		# ---- 8
		{
			when: freeps, choice, text(another move), turn(1)
			messages: [
				{
					text: The loser of a skirmish takes 1 wound.  Frodo is now down to {vitality:frodo} vitality, and in dire need of help.
					anchor: card:frodo:wounds
					highlightStyle: red
				}
				{
					text: "In the **Regroup Phase**, your fellowship must choose whether to continue traveling, or to hide.  \n\nIf you stay and hide, all minions on the table will be discarded, and you will **reconcile** your hand, drawing more cards.  \n\nLet's choose to stay; choose No on the pop-up."
					anchor: ui:dialog
					avoid: card:frodo
				}
			]
			allow: option(No)
		}
		# ---- 9
		{
			note: TURN 2: site 2 to site 3, with Gandalf
			checkpoint: true
			when: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: "Now you have reconciled your hand, drawing some cards!  \n\n(In a real game, reconciling has a much bigger impact, but we are skipping over those rules for now.)"
					anchor: zone:self.hand
					highlight: zone:self.hand
					side: above
				}
				{
					text: "Since you chose to stay, it is now the **Fellowship Phase** once again.  This is your chance to play companions and other cards.\n\nYou've drawn Gandalf!  Gandalf is a companion who costs {cost:gandalf}; a hefty sum but a Wizard is always worth it.\n\nClick on Gandalf to play him from hand."
					anchor: card:gandalf
					highlight: card:gandalf
					side: above
				}
			]
			allow: play(gandalf)
		}
		# ---- 10
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: Gandalf now joins Frodo on his journey.  Your fellowship is growing!
					anchor: card:gandalf
					highlight: card:gandalf
				}
				{
					text: Like Minions, Companions have a **Twilight Cost** in the upper left corner of the card.
					zoom: card:gandalf
					focus: cost
				}
				{
					text: Because Gandalf is a Free Peoples card, you have put 4 tokens *into* the Twilight Pool, which will be used later by your opponent to pay for their minions.
					anchor: ui:twilightPool
					highlight: ui:twilightPool
				}
				{
					text: These other cards are Events.  They represent moments of bravery, luck, or skill, and we will have a chance to use them later.
					anchor: zone:self.hand
					highlight: zone:self.hand
					side: above
				}
				{
					text: Click Pass to end the Fellowship Phase.
					anchor: ui:button:pass
					highlight: ui:button:pass
				}
			]
			allow: pass
		}
		# ---- 11
		{
			when: opponent, action, phase(shadow), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: "The fellowship has made it to [[Rivendell Valley]] at Site 3.\n\nRivendell has a Shadow Number of (0), but we still add (1) per companion, putting us at ({twilight}) total after paying for Gandalf and moving.\n\nNext your opponent will have a chance to play cards during the **Shadow Phase**."
					anchor: ui:twilightPool
					highlight: ui:twilightPool, ui:site:3
					side: right
				}
			]
			answer: play(soldier)
		}
		# ---- 12
		{
			when: opponent, action, phase(shadow), turn(2)
			answer: play(chieftain)
		}
		# ---- 13
		{
			when: shadow, action, phase(shadow), turn(2)
			answer: pass
		}
		# ---- 14
		{
			when: freeps, assign, turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: "There are no archers this time, so we proceed to the **Assignment Phase**.\n\nSince there are 2 minions, we will have to assign them to 2 companions.  \n\nAssign the Soldier to Gandalf."
					anchor: card:soldier
					avoid: card:gandalf, card:frodo, card:chieftain
					side: right
				}
				{
					text: Next, assign the Chieftain to Frodo.
					anchor: card:chieftain
					avoid: card:frodo
					on: assigned(gandalf)
				}
				{
					text: Click Done to lock in these assignments.
					anchor: ui:button:done
					on: ready
				}
			]
			allow: assign(gandalf: soldier, frodo: chieftain)
		}
		# ---- 15
		{
			when: freeps, cards, text(next skirmish), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: Now that there are two skirmishes, you must decide which order to perform them in.  Let's do Gandalf's skirmish first.
					anchor: ui:assignment:gandalf
					side: left
				}
			]
			allow: choose(gandalf)
		}
		# ---- 16
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(skirmish), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: "Some skirmishes are so one-sided that the loser has no chance of getting away.  If one side **doubles** the strength of the other at the end of a skirmish, the loser is **overwhelmed** and immediately dies, indicated here by the red strength total.\n\nThe Soldier here has 2 vitality, which means it should be able to take a hit, but because his strength is less than half of Gandalf's, he won't survive the fight."
					anchor: ui:skirmish:shadowStrength
					highlight: ui:skirmish:shadowStrength
				}
				{
					text: Click Pass to end the skirmish and put the Orc in the ground.
					anchor: ui:button:pass
					highlight: ui:button:pass
				}
			]
			allow: {
				answers: pass
				otherwise: Gandalf doesn't need any help with this one. Save your Events for a fight that does.
			}
		}
		# ---- 17
		{
			when: shadow, action, phase(skirmish), turn(2)
			answer: pass
		}
		# ---- 18
		{
			when: freeps, cards, text(next skirmish), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: Now it's time for Frodo to fight.
					anchor: ui:assignment:frodo
				}
			]
			allow: choose(frodo)
		}
		# ---- 19
		{
			note: Either copy will do.  The ? says "if it is on offer": by the next step one of them has been played.
			when: freeps, action, phase(skirmish), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: Frodo is in trouble, and is in danger of being overwhelmed.  His {strength:frodo} strength isn't enough to survive against the Chieftain's {strength:chieftain}!  Let's play an Event to rescue him.
					anchor: ui:skirmish
					highlight: ui:skirmish:fpStrength, ui:skirmish:shadowStrength
				}
				{
					text: "**Events** are cards that you play once and then discard, getting whatever bonuses their text says until the end of the current phase.\n\nEvents will say in their game text or type bar when they can be played.  [[Servant of the Secret Fire]] has a bold **Skirmish** in its game text, and it is the Skirmish phase, so now is the perfect time.\n\n\"**Spot** X\" means that X must be on the table and active.  We can spot Gandalf, so we are permitted to play this now."
					zoom: card:servant1
					focus: text
				}
				{
					text: Let's play a copy of [[Servant of the Secret Fire]].
					anchor: card:servant1
					highlight: card:gandalf
				}
			]
			allow: play(servant1)?, play(servant2)?
			answer: play(servant1)
		}
		# ---- 20
		{
			when: opponent, action, phase(skirmish), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: The Chieftain has been reduced from 9 to {strength:chieftain} strength.  Frodo may survive this yet!
					anchor: card:chieftain
					highlight: card:chieftain:strength
					side: left
				}
			]
			answer: play(drums1)
		}
		# ---- 21
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(skirmish), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: "Oh no!  Your opponent played an event of their own!  Look down here in the **Combat Log** to see it.  \n\nYou can click or hover over the name of a card to see what was played if you missed it.  If you need to, you can scroll up to see a log of everything that's happened recently."
					anchor: ui:gameLog
					highlight: ui:gameLog
					highlightStyle: blue
					avoid: zone:self.support
					side: above
				}
				{
					text: **[[Drums in the Deep]]** made the Chieftain strength +2.  Frodo is once more in danger of being overwhelmed.  Let's play the second copy of [[Servant of the Secret Fire]].
					anchor: zone:self.hand
					highlight: zone:self.hand
				}
			]
			allow: play(servant1)?, play(servant2)?
			answer: play(servant2)
		}
		# ---- 22
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(skirmish), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: Phew, our opponent didn't play another event.  Frodo will lose his skirmish, but live to fight another day.
					anchor: ui:skirmish
					highlight: ui:button:pass
				}
				{
					text: Click Pass to end the skirmish.
					anchor: ui:button:pass
					highlight: ui:button:pass
				}
			]
			allow: pass
		}
		# ---- 23
		{
			when: shadow, cards, phase(regroup), turn(2)
			answer: pass
		}
		# ---- 24
		{
			when: freeps, choice, text(another move), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: "Frodo took 1 wound and avoided being overwhelmed.  \n\nHowever, he is now **exhausted**--only 1 wound away from death.  Some cards will punish you for being exhausted, but more importantly, he's almost dead!"
					anchor: card:frodo:vitality
					highlight: card:frodo:wounds
					highlightStyle: red
					side: below
					gap: 5
				}
				{
					text: "It is now the **Regroup Phase**.  \n\nWith Frodo like this, you are in no state to keep running.  Time to hide from these Orcs, and reconcile our hand again."
					anchor: ui:dialog
					avoid: card:frodo
				}
			]
			allow: option(No)
		}
		# ---- 25
		{
			note: The game asks this whenever you reconcile with cards in hand, so it has to be answered.
			when: freeps, cards, text(Reconcile), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: "Normally when you reconcile, you may first discard 1 card from your hand, to make room for more when you draw.  \n\nHowever, we want to keep all of these, so click Done."
					anchor: ui:button:done
					highlight: ui:button:done
					side: above
				}
			]
			allow: pass
		}
		# ---- 26
		{
			note: TURN 3: site 3 to site 4, the whole fellowship
			checkpoint: true
			when: freeps, cards, text(Sanctuary healing)
			until: freeps, action
			messages: [
				{
					text: "It is the start of the **Fellowship Phase** once more!  \n\nRivendell is a **sanctuary**, which you can tell by its grey color.  All site 3s and site 6s are sanctuaries, which are a place where you can rest and heal.  \n\nAt the start of your Fellowship Phase after you choose to stay at a sanctuary, you may heal up to 5 wounds from your companions, so click on Frodo to heal him up!"
					anchor: card:frodo
					highlight: ui:site:3
				}
			]
			allow: choose(frodo)
			answer: choose(frodo), choose(frodo), choose(frodo)
		}
		# ---- 27
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(between_turns), turn(3), text(Optional responses)
			messages: [
				{
					text: After sanctuary healing, your usual turn starts.  Gandalf has game text that lets you draw an extra card at the start of your turn.
					anchor: card:gandalf:text
					highlight: card:gandalf:text
				}
				{
					text: Since this is an optional trigger ("you **may** draw a card"), you have the option to pass.  But why give up a free card?
					anchor: ui:button:pass
					highlight: ui:button:pass
				}
				{
					text: Click on Gandalf to activate his optional trigger.
					anchor: card:gandalf
					highlight: card:gandalf
				}
			]
			allow: use(gandalf)
		}
		# ---- 28
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(3)
			until: phase(shadow)
			messages: [
				{
					text: "And now it is time to play more companions.  Add Aragorn and Boromir to the fellowship.\n\nClick Pass once you are ready to move on."
					anchor: zone:self.hand
					highlight: card:aragorn, card:boromir
					side: above
				}
			]
			allow: {
				answers: play(aragorn), play(boromir)
				passWhen: [
					{
						type: canSpot
						filter: alias(aragorn)
					}
					{
						type: canSpot
						filter: alias(boromir)
					}
				]
				otherwise: Both Aragorn and Boromir are coming with us. Play the two of them first.
			}
			answer: play(aragorn), play(boromir), pass
		}
